When a stylesheet link is disabled, Ladybird keeps its sheet aside,
and puts it back if the link is enabled again before it starts another
fetch. The other engines drop the sheet when the link is disabled,
and load it again when the link is enabled, which their memory caches
answer: Blink’s LinkStyle::SetDisabledState() clears the sheet and
calls Process(), WebKit’s HTMLLinkElement::setDisabledState() calls
clearSheet() and process(), and Gecko’s HTMLLinkElement::AfterSetAttr()
forces UpdateStyleSheetInternal().
